{"kind":"text","seq":45,"text":"Best banked result this round is confirmed. Four builds were tested:\n\n| Build | Pieces | Length | Inversions | Intensity | Excitement |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1: loop + corkscrews, short return | 71 | 467 | 2 | 8.63 | 6.09 |\n| 2: added half loop + second loop | 88 | 580 | 4 | 9.87 | 6.66 |\n| 3: long hill run to x=90 | 137 | 818 | 4 | 10.54 | 5.20 |\n| 4: fewer drops, slower banked turn | 115 | 714 | 4 | 9.93 | **6.87** |\n\nBuild 3 showed the ceiling clearly: extra hills pushed intensity past 10 and excitement collapsed. Build 4 kept the four inversions, cut the drop count back to ten, and used flats and brakes on the loop-back leg to stay just under the limit. Similarity to the stock library is 0.39, so no penalty applied. Nothing was named or coloured.\n\nBest coaster: 115-piece twister with a 12-tile lift into a 60° drop, vertical loop, corkscrew pair, boosted half loop with corkscrew, and a second vertical loop, closing via banked turns south of the lake. Excitement 6.87, intensity 9.93, nausea 5.76."}
